From b5238f9e59be2be85766d5277570f5d521ae1f0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: y700 workspace <304558835+bobsixsixsix-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: baldur-stats: hand qcom_stats the AOSS QMP

On SM8450 and later the AOP fills in the duration fields of the DDR
statistics only when asked: qcom_ddr_stats_show() sends
"{class: ddr, action: freqsync}" before reading MSG RAM, but only when
the rpmh-stats node has a qcom,qmp phandle. Without it ddr_stats reads
"Duration (ticks):0" for every DDR low-power mode and frequency, so
there is no way to tell whether DDR self-refresh is ever reached with
the screen off.

sm8750.dtsi has the property on the same node, and so do the
kaanapali.dtsi of infiniti-mainline and of the OnePlus Pad 4 tree
(SuperTurtleDev/iceland-mainline-kernel-linux 03896b28).

Side effects: qcom_stats now defers its probe until aoss_qmp is up
(CONFIG_QCOM_AOSS_QMP=y here) and fails the probe on any other
qmp_get() error, which would take every qcom_stats file with it; each
read of ddr_stats sends one QMP message and waits up to 1 s for the
AOP to take it. The other files (apss, cxsd, aosd, ddr, subsystems) are
read as before.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-stats.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-stats.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-stats.dtsi
index 26b710a..0e30a6b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-stats.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/baldur-stats.dtsi
@@ -9,5 +9,6 @@
 	sram@c3f0000 {
 		compatible = "qcom,rpmh-stats";
 		reg = <0x0 0x0c3f0000 0x0 0x400>;
+		qcom,qmp = <&aoss_qmp>;
 	};
 };
